Therefore, to train a Machine Learning model with Scikit-Learn, this will always be done in the same way in 4 lines of code:
============================================================================================================================

# Instancing of the chosen model 
# To create a model, we generate an object of the class corresponding to this object
# LinearRegression is a regression algorithm
# We can specify some parameters of the algorithm between the brackets.

model = LinearRegression() 

# Model training on the training dataset

model.fit(X_train,y_train) 

# Prediction of the target variable for the testing dataest, these predictions are stored in y_pred

y_pred = model.predict(X_test) 

# Evaluation of the model: from X_test, we predict the target variable that we compare to y_test

model.score(X_test,y_test)
Whether to develop a classification or regression algorithm, this will be almost always in the same way.
